  "reason": "Evidence: config_051 (scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, concat, multiprofile) is the current best at 0.715 acc, and with pca_n2000, avgpool outperformed transformer aggregation by ~3% (0.629 vs 0.599). However, we have no evidence on whether this aggregation preference holds with the substantially stronger scvi_n200 encoder. Question: config_017 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer (keeping scvi_n200, vit_l, concat, multiprofile), cleanly isolating whether a more expressive aggregation mechanism can exploit the richer scvi_n200 representation. Why best next: It is a single-variable comparison directly against the current best, tests an important design axis at the performance frontier, and the outcome (whether transformer helps or hurts) will either open a new exploitation direction or confirm avgpool as the robust choice, reducing uncertainty about aggregation before committing further experiments."
